.TH AVR\-RUN\-RERUN 1 "" "avr 0.6.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-run-rerun \- Re-run a completed workflow run.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr run rerun
[OPTIONS] RUN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Re-run a completed workflow run.
.PP
RUN accepts the same Avrea IDs, GitHub run IDs, and run URLs as `avr run view`.
.PP
Avrea CI keeps the original revision. Use --failed for failed/cancelled jobs or repeat --job for selected jobs. Their downstream dependents also rerun; other results are retained. The new attempt can be watched immediately.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr run rerun run-019e5a2e474e71c297e452279d4bcdea
    avr run rerun run-019e5a2e474e71c297e452279d4bcdea --failed
    avr run rerun run-019e5a2e474e71c297e452279d4bcdea --yes
    avr run rerun awr-019e5a2e474e71c297e452279d4bcdea --job build --job test
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIRUN\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug.
.TP
\fB\-\-failed\fR
Re-run failed jobs and dependents; includes cancelled jobs for Avrea CI.
.TP
\fB\-\-job\fR \fITEXT\fR
Avrea job name or ID to rerun with dependents; repeat for multiple jobs. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fIUUID\fR
Reuse a previous Avrea CI rerun request UUID.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
